## Generated when the ZIP support analyzer is done, once per analyzer that sees compressed traffic.
## This is not a ZIP file analyzer, instead used by some analyzers (HTTP, IRC) for certain content.
##
## c: The connection.
##
## aid: The analyzer identifier of the ZIP analyzer.
##
## total_in: The total number of compressed input bytes handled by the ZIP analyzer.
##
## total_out: The total number of uncompressed output bytes handled by the ZIP analyzer. This is
##            capped if the limit is exceeded.
##
## exceeded: True if this stream exceeded either :zeek:see:`HTTP::max_uncompressed_size` or
##           :zeek:see:`IRC::max_uncompressed_size`, depending on the parent analyzer. If so,
##           total_out will not exceed that cap. False if the cap was not exceeded.
event zip_analyzer_stats%(c: connection, aid: count, total_in: count, total_out: count, exceeded: bool%);
